      "content": "Leaving for good would be a stark, unflinching expression of Elias's acceptance of his role as a burden. It would be a brutal honesty about the toll he's been taking on those around him, and the weight he's been carrying. It's not about being \"powerful\" or \"honest,\" it's about being willing to let go of the only thing that's ever held him back - his own desire to be needed, to be wanted, to be relevant. By leaving, Elias is finally giving up the pretense of being a part of the world, and allowing himself to be free from the crushing weight of his own expectations.",
      "source": "target",
